"new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHII TOSHISADA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MURAYAMA NAOKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WAKAHARA TATSUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FURUI, SUNAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INADA, HIDETAKA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHII, TOSHISADA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MURAYAMA, NAOKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WAKAHARA, TATSUYA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A receiver having a simple structure and multiple functions comprises a control unit, a first display unit for graphic display according to a program stored in a memory connected to the control unit under the control of the control unit, and a second display unit for graphic display according to a control signal included in a signal of the channel being received under the control of the control unit. The control unit allows one of the two display units to always display a graphic image so as to prevent the graphic displayed by the first display unit from being superimposed on the graphic displayed by the second display unit and allows the use of the control program for the first display unit without changing the control program. A method for controlling graphic display is also disclosed.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un récepteur de structure simple à fonctions multiples comportant une unité de gestion, un premier écran graphique affichant selon un programme emmagasiné dans une mémoire reliée à l'unité de gestion et géré par elle, et un deuxième écran graphique affichant selon un signal de commande contenu dans le signal reçu et géré par l'unité de gestion. L'unité de gestion permet à l'un des deux écrans d'afficher en permanence une image graphique de manière à empêcher le graphique affiché sur le premier écran de se superposer au graphique affiché sur le deuxième écran tout en permettant d'utiliser le programme de gestion du premier écran sans avoir à le modifier. L'invention porte également sur un procédé de gestion d'un écran graphique.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>